# ============================================
# father_behan.dialogue
# ============================================
NPC: father_behan
LOCATION: rectory

TOPIC: sixth_man
  GATE: never
  # Permanently excluded. No line exists for this topic, on this NPC
  # or any other. Do not fill this in on a later pass.

TOPIC: club_five
  GATE: always
  LABEL: "Ask about the five club members"
  BEHAN: "Wexford's temper. Fenn's vanity. Kessler's grudges. Corliss's ambitions.
          I'll discuss any of it. None of it explains a hole above the bridge of a nose."
  CHOICE: "You knew all six."
    BEHAN: "I knew what men tell a priest, which is not the same as what they are.
            Ask your question, Officer. I've answered worse."

TOPIC: club_invitation
  GATE: always AND NOT topic_done(father_behan, club_invitation)
  LABEL: "Ask about the club invitations"
  CHOICE: "You were invited to the club. Twice. You declined both times."
    BEHAN: "I did."
  CHOICE: "Why?"
    BEHAN: [He says nothing further. The silence is not evasive. It is final.]
    NOTEBOOK: club_invitation_1_1 | "A refusal offered without excuse.
               Walter has learned to trust a plain no more than a decorated one."

# Reverse-engineered from town_story.gd SCENES.behan_name. _behan_menu()
# shows this button INSTEAD OF club_invitation's once that one is answered
# (never both at once); "NOT topic_done(...)" on club_invitation above and
# "topic_done(...)" here reproduce that mutually exclusive reveal exactly.
TOPIC: behan_name
  GATE: topic_done(father_behan, club_invitation)
  LABEL: "Ask about the meaning of the club's name"
  WALTER CORWIN: "Do you know the meaning behind the club's name?"
  FATHER BEHAN: "They named the club after the ship."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Known."
  FATHER BEHAN: "They came to believe the ship had been chosen.\n\nIt wasn't. Men inherit money, and then invent a reason they deserved it."
  NOTEBOOK: behan_name_1_1 | "NAMED AFTER THE SHIP\n\nThe Ophion Club was named for a vessel lost with its crew a century ago. Father Behan calls the members' belief that the ship had been chosen a delusion, not a fact: men inherit money, then invent a reason they deserved it.\n\nFather Behan · rectory conversation"
  NOTEBOOK: "A shipowner's classical flourish, nothing more, by the priest's own account.\n\nThe club's fortune has a human explanation. Walter intends to find it."

TOPIC: bullets
  GATE: always
  LABEL: "Ask about the bullet wound"
  CHOICE: "Have you ever heard of a bullet that leaves no exit wound?"
    BEHAN: [A pause held a beat too long.] "Ask your question, Officer. I've answered worse."
    # deliberately reuses his own stock line — the second use reads as evasion,
    # not repetition, once the player's heard it land honestly once already
